; vulkanTripleResourceProof.pi4 - public sample * push + UBO Vulkan path,
;                                 drawn by V3D on Pi 4.
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. IT DOES NOT SHIP. It is an instrument, not a how-to.
;
;   PureMetalForge.exe --compile \
;       RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/vulkanTripleResourceProof.pi4 -t pi4 \
;       --load-addr 0x500000 --stack-addr 0x4F00000 --entry-returns \
;       -o vulkanTripleResourceProof.img
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHAT IT PROVES, ON THE SILICON
; ======================================================================
;  vulkanTriangleProof.pi4 proved that a SPIR-V module chooses the
;  shaders and that one triangle goes through the pipeline. Its second
;  pass gave all three vertices the SAME colour on purpose, so it proved
;  the varying PATH and nothing about interpolation. This proves the
;  four things that came next, and each is a different question:
;
;    PASS A - A UNIFORM BUFFER FEEDS THE FRAGMENT COLOUR, through the
;             whole descriptor path: vkCreateDescriptorSetLayout,
;             vkCreatePipelineLayout with it, vkCreateDescriptorPool,
;             vkAllocateDescriptorSets, vkUpdateDescriptorSets with a
;             VkDescriptorBufferInfo, and vkCmdBindDescriptorSets. The
;             fragment module declares `layout(set = 0, binding = 0)
;             uniform U { vec4 colour; }` and reads member zero through
;             an OpAccessChain. A solid magenta triangle: exact, because
;             every component is 0.0 or 1.0.
;
;    PASS B - A REAL GRADIENT. The same geometry with THREE DIFFERENT
;             per-vertex colours - red at the apex, green at the lower
;             left, blue at the lower right - carried through the VPM as
;             a varying and read back with LDVARY. Seven probe pixels,
;             each with an expected colour computed from the barycentric
;             weights at that pixel's own centre.
;
;    PASS C - THE SAME GRADIENT OUT OF TWO VERTEX BUFFERS. Position in
;             one buffer at a stride of eight bytes, colour in another
;             at a stride of sixteen, two vertex input bindings. The
;             expected pixels are PASS B's, and the verdict includes
;             "every probe is the same word as pass B's": splitting the
;             data across two buffers must change where the vertex
;             fetcher reads and nothing whatever about the picture.
;
;    PASS D - ONE PUBLIC TYPED-IR FRAGMENT computes sample(binding 1)
;             * push + UBO(binding 0). A
;             separate 4x4 optimal-tiled BGRA8 image is populated from a
;             host-visible transfer buffer by vkCmdCopyBufferToImage and a
;             real V3D TFU job, transitioned to shader-read layout, resolved
;             through a closed descriptor and sampled by real TMU requests.
;             The push scale is 0.5 and the UBO adds (0.5,0,0,1), so
;             source red/green/blue become exact $FFFF0000/$FF808000/
;             $FF800080. Three exact inside colours, three exact outside
;             pixels, metadata, lifetime reuse, TFU/bin/render counters and
;             zero fault state make the result exact.
;
;  SEVEN SPIR-V MODULES ARE ASSEMBLED WORD BY WORD, from the Khronos
;  specification's own opcode numbers, in
;  Anvil/Graphics/Vulkan/vk_spirv_fixtures.pbi - the same file the
;  triangle proof uses, and the same file tools/vulkan_pipeline_check.py
;  compares word for word against a Python assembler at the desk.
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHERE THE EXPECTED GRADIENT PIXELS COME FROM
; ======================================================================
;  Anvil/Graphics/Vulkan/vk_interp_expect.pbi. It is integer arithmetic
;  with no floating point in it at all: the clip-to-screen transform in
;  units of 1/256 of a pixel, the three edge functions at the centre of
;  the probe's own pixel, the weighted average of the three vertex
;  colours, and one rounded division into an 8-bit UNORM. This payload
;  calls it and puts its answers in the report beside the pixels the GPU
;  produced, so a reader never has to take the expectation on trust.
;
;  tools/vulkan_interp_check.py runs that same module at a desk over
;  eight triangles and thirty-three probes and compares every number
;  against a second implementation of the rule written in Python, and
;  rejects fourteen mutations of it. THE BOARD IS NOT THE FIRST PLACE
;  THESE NUMBERS ARE CHECKED.
;
;  THE TOLERANCE IS TWO 8-BIT STEPS PER CHANNEL, and it is not zero
;  because the hardware is not exact: V3D delivers a varying through
;  LDVARY as a binary32 built from a per-primitive slope and a
;  per-fragment step, the fragment shader packs two lanes into one
;  2 x f16 result, and the tile buffer converts that to 8-bit UNORM.
;  Eleven mantissa bits is about a fifth of one 8-bit step. Two is small
;  enough that it cannot hide a real defect: a varying wired to the
;  wrong component, a missing interpolation or a flat fill all miss by
;  tens or hundreds. The report carries the WORST distance and the
;  number of probes over tolerance, so a marginal run is visible as one.
;
;  THE THREE PROBES NEAREST THE VERTICES ARE INSET 40 PIXELS along the
;  median towards the centroid, and that is deliberate: a probe at a
;  vertex sits on two edges at once, where the rasteriser's fill rule
;  and not arithmetic decides whether it is covered. Inset, each is
;  dominated by its own vertex by more than 200 of 255 - which is what
;  makes this run able to tell a gradient from a flat fill at all.
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHAT THE OPERATOR SHOULD SEE
; ======================================================================
;  A sharply divided olive/red/magenta triangle, apex up, on a blue-grey
;  ground, held for one second. These are nearest-filter samples from the
;  4x4 optimal-tiled image: green at the apex, blue at the lower left and
;  red at the lower right. In panel pixels the apex is at (400, 320) and
;  the base runs from (200, 960) to (600, 960).
;
;  That is PASS D - the colour sampled through the combined image
;  descriptor. Passes A, B and C are drawn into the same image first and
;  overwritten by the following pass's clear, so they live in the report.
;
;  AN OPERATOR WHO SEES A GRADIENT OR SOLID MAGENTA TRIANGLE has watched
;  a run where pass D did not replace the previous pass, and slot 125 says
;  which step stopped it. A solid sampled triangle is the old one-texel
;  proof, not this optimal-image transfer proof.
;
; ======================================================================
;  BEFORE RUNNING IT
; ======================================================================
;  * TAKE THE ACCELERATED CONSOLE OFF V3D FIRST: `screen dma`. This
;    payload initialises the graphics engine itself and uses the SAME
;    16 MiB arena at $0A000000 that the V3D console vets and owns; two
;    owners of one V3D page table is not a thing that can be made to
;    work.
;  * THE BUFFERS ARE IN THE PAYLOAD WINDOW at $06000000: one screen of
;    guard and one screen plus 128 KiB of Vulkan window, 8,323,072 bytes
;    ending at $067EF000 - the same band vulkanClearProof.pi4 and
;    vulkanTriangleProof.pi4 already used.
;  * IT DOES NOT RE-INITIALISE THE DISPLAY and asks the firmware for
;    nothing. It adopts the scanout buffer for the length of one copy.
;  * IT CALLS NeonShutdown() BEFORE RETURNING, which hands the V3D MMU
;    back.
;  * RECOVERY: the console repaints over the presented picture by
;    itself; `screen on` forces it and `screen v3d` brings the
;    accelerated console back. Neither needs a reset. Nothing here
;    writes a core spin slot, releases a core, or touches the monitor,
;    its variables, the DSI control registers, the GENET ring or the
;    driver-module region.
;
; ======================================================================
;  THE REPORT, AND HOW TO READ IT
; ======================================================================
;  x0 comes back as the address of TWO HUNDRED AND FORTY 32-BIT
;  WORDS - 960 bytes. ONE SLOT IS ONE WORD, so the slot number below is
;  the word number in the dump. Read it with
;
;      md.l <x0> 3C0
;
;  and NOT with a bare `md`: the dump's count is in BYTES whichever
;  width is chosen, so 3C0 hex is 960 bytes is 240 words, and a bare
;  `md` groups by one byte. 3C0 is written in hex because every
;  argument of that command is.
;
;  Slot 0 is $59524156 ("VARY") and slot 239 is $56415259, the same four
;  letters backwards. A dump that does not show BOTH did not show the
;  whole report, and the verdicts near the end of it were not read.
;
;     0  magic $59524156 ("VARY")
;     1  PASS A VERDICT - the uniform-buffer colour
;     2  PASS B VERDICT - the gradient out of one buffer
;     3  PASS C VERDICT - the gradient out of two buffers
;     4  detail; render control-list current address when submit A fails
;     5  detail 2; render control-list status when submit A fails
;     6  surface (guard) base
;     7  Vulkan window base
;     8  Vulkan window bytes
;     9  image address
;    10  image size
;    11  image row pitch
;    12  interleaved vertex buffer address
;    13  position-only buffer address
;    14  colour-only buffer address
;    15  uniform buffer address
;    16  expected clear word, $FF3380B2
;    17  expected magenta word, $FFFF00FF
;    18  pipeline A code base (uniform colour)
;    19  pipeline B code base (gradient, one buffer)
;    20  pipeline C code base (gradient, two buffers)
;    21  triangle screen x0, in 1/256 of a pixel
;    22  triangle screen y0
;    23  triangle screen x1
;    24  triangle screen y1
;    25  triangle screen x2
;    26  triangle screen y2
;    27  twice the signed area, low 32 bits
;    28  the tolerance, 2
;    29  the gradient probe count, 7
;   30..36  EXPECTED gradient word, probes 0 to 6
;   37..39  pass A, inside: (400,500) (400,700) (400,900)
;   40..42  pass A, outside: (100,100) (700,1200) (400,200)
;   43..49  pass B, gradient probes 0 to 6
;   50..52  pass B, the three outside probes
;    53  pass B worst distance, over all seven probes
;    54  pass B probes over tolerance
;   55..61  pass C, gradient probes 0 to 6
;   62..64  pass C, the three outside probes
;    65  linear-format feature bits reported for B8G8R8A8_UNORM
;    66  host-visible allocations populated through vkMapMemory, must be 5
;    67  pass C worst distance
;    68  pass C probes over tolerance
;    69  probes where pass C differs from pass B - must be 0
;    70  refusal: an attribute names an undescribed binding
;    71  its sentence
;    72  refusal: a storage image descriptor type
;    73  its sentence
;    74  refusal: a uniform draw with no descriptor set bound
;    75  its sentence
;    76  refusal: a uniform shader on a layout with no set layout
;    77  its sentence
;    78  bin jobs before
;    79  bin jobs after
;    80  render jobs before
;    81  render jobs after
;    82  bin OOM count
;    83  bin error status
;    84  render error status
;    85  MMU fault count
;    86  MMU violation address
;    87  guard sum before
;    88  guard sum after
;    89  submit result, pass A
;    90  wait result, pass A
;    91  submit result, pass B
;    92  wait result, pass B
;    93  submit result, pass C
;    94  wait result, pass C
;    95  backend native error
;    96  validation fault count
;    97  validation fault text
;    98  PRESENT VERDICT
;    99  DisplayLastError()
;   100  engine arena needed
;   101  backend can draw
;   102  backend name
;   103  image layout after
;   104  microseconds, submit A
;   105  microseconds, submit B
;   106  microseconds, submit C
;   107  draws the backend ran
;   108  last shader record address
;   109  command buffer failure text
;   110  shutdown reached
;   111  emitter step, if a pipeline was refused
;   112  encoder code if a pipeline was refused; render control-list end
;        address when submit A fails
;   113  the descriptor address the draw resolved to
;   114  the descriptor range
;   115  pipeline C binding 0 stride, 8
;   116  pipeline C binding 1 stride, 16
;   117  pipeline C attribute 0 binding, 0
;   118  pipeline C attribute 1 binding, 1
;   119  pipeline C binding count, 2
;   120  descriptor fragment-program bytes, 144
;   121  descriptor fragment stream word 0: uniform-buffer address
;   122  descriptor fragment stream word 1: TMU general vec4 config
;   123  descriptor fragment stream word 2: TLB config
;   124  descriptor GPU-lowering evidence verdict, 1
;   125  HIGHEST STEP REACHED, 1 to 13
;   126  report length in bytes, 960
;   127  reserved
;   128  PASS D VERDICT - combined image sampler
;   129  sampled image address
;   130  sampled pipeline code base
;   131  sampled draw submit result
;   132  sampled draw fence-wait result
; 133..135  sampled pass inside pixels
; 136..138  sampled pass outside pixels
;   139  sampled fragment-program bytes
; 140..142  texture-state, sampler-state and TLB uniform words
; 143..146  texture base, width, height and format/swizzle state words
; 147..148  sampler-state words
; 149..150  bin jobs before and after sampled draw
; 151..152  render jobs before and after sampled draw
; 153..155  sampled draw MMU faults, bin OOM and native backend error
;   156  sampled failure detail
;   157  sampled shader-record address
;   158  total backend draws after sampled pass
; 159..160  TFU jobs before and after the optimal-image copy
;   161  transfer-source address (64-byte aligned offset in its buffer)
;   162  optimal image allocation bytes, including UIF padding
;   163  optimal image row pitch, zero because no linear pitch exists
; 164..165  copy submit and fence-wait results
;   166  layout after the successful copy, SHADER_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL
;   167  reserved
;   168  transfer buffer memoryTypeBits
;   169  selected host-visible memory type
;   170  selected memory property flags
;   171  physical memory type count
;   172  transfer buffer allocation bytes
;   173  VkMemoryAllocateInfo sType at the call boundary
;   174  transfer buffer vkAllocateMemory result
; 176..188  source module/layout slots and generations before/after reuse
; 189..199  pre/post synchronous-submit in-flight counters (all zero after)
; 200..213  push words and exact lowerer metadata indices
; 214..216  cumulative fault counts and pass-D elapsed microseconds (<15,000,000)
; 217..220  expected mixed pixels and exact-match verdict
; 221..222  exact bin/render deltas, one each
; 224..233  patched uniform words and UBO-config metadata index
; 234..235  fault codes after the two one-write descriptor updates
;   236  optimal texture-state word 4, $40 (strict UIF)
; 237..238  current fault code before/after the mixed draw (both OK)
;   239  tail magic $56415259
;
;  THE PROBE PIXELS, in panel coordinates:
;    0 (400, 346)  inset from the apex          - red dominant
;    1 (213, 946)  inset from the lower left    - green dominant
;    2 (587, 946)  inset from the lower right   - blue dominant
;    3 (400, 747)  the centroid                 - equal thirds
;    4 (400, 500)  high on the median
;    5 (300, 800)  left of centre, low
;    6 (500, 800)  right of centre, low
;  and three OUTSIDE it, which must still hold the clear colour:
;    (100, 100), (700, 1200), (400, 200)
;
;  SLOT 125 IS THE ONE TO READ FIRST when anything is wrong. It is the
;  number of the step that was running, 1 to 13, and 13 means the whole
;  payload ran including present, teardown and final whole-run checks.
;
;  THE EXPECTED BYTES. VK_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_UNORM stores B, G, R, A in
;  ascending byte order, so a 32-bit word read on this little-endian
;  part is (A<<24)|(R<<16)|(G<<8)|B.
;      clear     R 0.2 G 0.5 B 0.7 A 1.0   ->  $FF3380B2
;      magenta   R 1.0 G 0.0 B 1.0 A 1.0   ->  $FFFF00FF
;  The gradient's seven expected words are not constants here - they are
;  computed on the board and reported in slots 30 to 36, and the desk
;  gate has already checked the module that computes them.
;
;  THERE IS NO PROCESSOR-SIDE FALLBACK ANYWHERE UNDER THIS. If V3D does
;  not rasterise and interpolate, the readback fails.
;
; ======================================================================
;  THE NEW PIECE THIS RUN MUST PROVE
; ======================================================================
;  THE TEXTURE IS NO LONGER A MAPPED LINEAR ONE-TEXEL SHORTCUT. The core
;  command records one tightly packed whole-image buffer-to-image copy.
;  Submission revalidates both live resources and bindings, retains them
;  through completion, runs the V3D TFU into UIF_NO_XOR optimal layout and
;  publishes SHADER_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL only after success. The fragment
;  shader then samples that >1x1 result through the ordinary descriptor.
;
;  The report makes each ownership layer independently visible: slots
;  159..166 cover TFU execution, source address, padded image extent and
;  layout publication; slots 168..174 cover the public memory selection
;  and allocation call; slots 133..148 cover exact pixels and the V3D 4.2
;  texture/sampler state. Slots 176..233 cover source-object destruction and
;  same-slot generation reuse, all nine post-submit release counters, exact
;  lowerer-returned metadata and uniform words, no new mixed-path faults and
;  the 15-second deadman. The cumulative count is five intentional refusal
;  probes made earlier; slots 237..238 prove the current code is clear. No
;  processor-side image write or fallback exists.

XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/uart.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/timer.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/safety.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/mailbox.pi4"
#DSP_DMA_LINKED = 0
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/display.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3dqpu.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3d.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/neon.pi4"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Graphics/Vulkan/vk_api.pbi"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Graphics/Vulkan/vk_spirv_fixtures.pbi"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Graphics/Vulkan/vk_interp_expect.pbi"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Graphics/Vulkan/vk_v3d_shader.pi4"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Graphics/Vulkan/vk_v3d_backend.pi4"

#VVP_MAGIC = $59524156                 ; "VARY", slot 0
#VVP_TAIL_MAGIC = $56415259            ; "YRAV", final report slot
#VVP_REPORT_BYTES = 240 * 4

#VVP_ARENA = $0A000000
#VVP_ARENA_BYTES = $01000000

#VVP_SURFACE = $06000000
#VVP_PANEL_W = 800
#VVP_PANEL_H = 1280
#VVP_PANEL_PITCH = 3200
#VVP_SCREEN_BYTES = 4096000
#VVP_WIN_BASE = $063E8000              ; $06000000 + 4,096,000
#VVP_WIN_BYTES = 4227072               ; one screen plus 128 KiB
#VVP_MAP_SPAN = 8323072
#VVP_DSI_SCAN = $08A00000

#VVP_GUARD = $5A3C0FF0

#VVP_F_ZERO = $00000000
#VVP_F_ONE = $3F800000
#VVP_CLEAR_R = $3E4CCCCD               ; 0.2 -> 51
#VVP_CLEAR_G = $3F000000               ; 0.5 -> 128
#VVP_CLEAR_B = $3F333333               ; 0.7 -> 178
#VVP_CLEAR_A = $3F800000               ; 1.0 -> 255
#VVP_CLEAR_WORD = $FF3380B2
#VVP_MAGENTA_WORD = $FFFF00FF
#VVP_TEXTURE_WORD = $FFFFC020           ; opaque R=255, G=192, B=32
#VVP_TEX_RED = $FFFF0000
#VVP_TEX_GREEN = $FF00FF00
#VVP_TEX_BLUE = $FF0000FF
#VVP_TEX_YELLOW = $FFFFFF00
#VVP_MIX_RED = $FFFF0000              ; sample red * .5 + UBO(.5,0,0,1)
#VVP_MIX_GREEN = $FF808000            ; sample green * .5 + UBO(.5,0,0,1)
#VVP_MIX_BLUE = $FF800080             ; sample blue * .5 + UBO(.5,0,0,1)
#VVP_TMU_GENERAL_VEC4 = $FFFFFF7C

; The triangle, in clip space. +Y is DOWN, which is Vulkan's framebuffer
; orientation and the V3D rasteriser's. The expectation module is told
; the same three vertices as exact rationals, so the geometry the report
; predicts and the geometry the GPU draws come from one set of numbers.
#VVP_X0 = $00000000                    ;  0.0
#VVP_Y0 = $BF000000                    ; -0.5
#VVP_X1 = $BF000000                    ; -0.5
#VVP_Y1 = $3F000000                    ;  0.5
#VVP_X2 = $3F000000                    ;  0.5
#VVP_Y2 = $3F000000                    ;  0.5

; The three layouts. The interleaved one is a vec2 position followed by
; a vec4 colour; the split pair is the same data in two buffers.
#VVP_STRIDE_ALL = 24
#VVP_STRIDE_POS = 8
#VVP_STRIDE_COL = 16
#VVP_UNIFORM_BYTES = 16

; Keep the complete three-pass run inside Anvil's hardware-deadman ceiling.
; The screenshot-on-return gate preserves the frame; a six-second hold could
; make the watchdog reset the payload before its report exposed a failure.
#VVP_SHOW_MS = 1000

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE VERDICTS. Slots 1, 2 and 3 all use these codes.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#VVP_OK = 0
#VVP_NOT_TRIED = 1
#VVP_ERR_NEON = 6
#VVP_ERR_WINDOW = 7
#VVP_ERR_INSTANCE = 8
#VVP_ERR_DEVICE = 9
#VVP_ERR_IMAGE = 10
#VVP_ERR_MEMORY = 11
